reference-kernel-ms 1.604, :workgroup-kernel-ms 0.288, :workgroup-gb-s 51.3}, :amd-8060s-gfx1151-radv-2026-09-18 {:reference-kernel-ms 0.557, :workgroup-kernel-ms 0.138, :workgroup-gb-s 107.0}, :nvidia-xavier-nvgpu-2026-09-18 {:reference-kernel-ms 19.06, :workgroup-kernel-ms 1.062, :workgroup-gb-s 13.9}, :backends-required [:intel-xpu :amd :apple-metal :nvidia], :backends-measured [:intel-xpu :amd :apple-metal :nvidia]}, :proves [:workgroup-per-row-q4-k-q8-k-dot :workgroup-per-row-q6-k-q8-k-dot :unaligned-q6-k-block-words :reference-parity-random-matrices :multi-position-parity :kernel-time-separated-from-submit-latency], :measures \"shaders/ggml_kdot_wg.wgsl against shaders/ggml_kdot.wgsl on the adapter Deno finds: ggml oracle on both, pseudo-random full-size Q4_K and Q6_K matrices at positions 1 and 3 through both, then K dispatches in one command buffer so the kernel's own time is separated from the 13-18 ms submit round trip that a single dispatch pays on Deno/wgpu. Root ADR-2609181800 M1: the first kernel in this ledger at llama.cpp-Vulkan-class bandwidth (100 GB/s on B70, 107 on AMD 8060S, 51 on M1 Max Metal, 14 on NVIDIA Xavier). Owner 2026-09-18: murakumo is not Metal-first -- every kernel gate carries all four backends (Intel XPU, AMD, Apple Metal, NVIDIA) in the same script, and a backend absent from :backends-measured is a red gate for that backend, not a skipped one.\", :does-not-prove \"Anything about the 42-layer generation path, which still dispatches the reference kernel from host/metal_kdot.cljk and pays one submit per projection; wiring the workgroup kernel into that host and cutting submits per token is M2.\"} {:id :decode-step-submit-shape, :kind :required-local-gpu, :command \"deno run --unstable-webgpu --allow-read verify/decode_step_bench.js\", :requires [:deno-webgpu :gpu-memory-8gib-free], :expected {:layers 42, :projections 302, :weights-gb 3.016, :b70-2026-09-18 {:A-per-projection-submit-ms 3930.5, :B-per-layer-submit-ms 39.2, :C-one-submit-ms 40.5, :A-over-C 97, :C-gb-s 74.5, :C-tok-s-floor 24.7}, :amd-8060s-2026-09-18 {:A-ms 3734.1, :B-ms 39.9, :C-ms 58.6, :C-min-ms 45.3, :A-over-C 63.7}, :m1-max-2026-09-18 {:A-ms 4414.6, :B-ms 72.6, :C-ms 71.8, :A-over-C 61.5}, :nvidia-xavier-2026-09-18 :unmeasured-node-serving-with-0.5-gib-free}, :proves [:submit-count-dominates-decode-latency :one-command-buffer-per-token-shape :weight-stream-floor-per-backend], :measures \"One Gemma4 e4b decode step's weight stream -- 42 x 7 projections at real shapes and ggml types plus the 262144 x 2560 Q6_K tied lm_head in eight 32768-row chunks -- through ggml_kdot_wg.wgsl with weights resident, in three submit shapes: A one submit + readback per projection (today's host), B one submit per layer, C one command buffer per token with a logits-only readback. Root ADR-2609181800 M2 / co-scientist iteration 1 hypothesis H1: the 8.4 s/token generation figure is submit count. Measured A/C = 97x on B70, 64x on AMD, 62x on Metal; shape A lands at 3.7-4.4 s/token on every backend, the order of the recorded 8.4 s.\", :does-not-prove \"tok/s for real generation: norms, attention, PLE, activation quantisation and sampling are not in this stream, so shape C is the weight-stream FLOOR of a decode step (24.7 tok/s on B70), not a rate. NVIDIA is unmeasured here because the only NVIDIA node serves nex with 0.5 GiB free.\"} {:id :q8k-quantize-parity, :kind :required-local-gpu, :command \"deno run --unstable-webgpu --allow-read verify/q8k_quantize_parity.js\", :requires [:deno-webgpu], :expected {:qs-mismatch 0, :bsums-mismatch 0, :d-ulp-max 2, :chain-dot-excess-over-tol-max 1e-4, :measured-2026-09-18 {:m1-max {:d-ulp 1, :perDispatch-ms-10240x3 0.0175}, :intel-b70 {:d-ulp 2, :perDispatch-ms-10240x3 0.0056}, :amd-8060s {:d-ulp 2, :perDispatch-ms-10240x3 0.011}, :nvidia-xavier :unmeasured}}, :proves [:gpu-q8-k-activation-quantisation :ggml-quantize-row-q8-k-parity :bsums-on-gpu :gpu-quantised-input-feeds-kdot-wg :zero-block-handling], :measures \"shaders/q8k_quantize.wgsl against a JS port of ggml quantize_row_q8_K_ref on pseudo-random rows (with an all-zero block), then the chain x -> GPU q8 -> ggml_kdot_wg versus x -> JS q8 -> ggml_kdot_wg. qs and bsums are exact on every backend; d differs by the backend`s f32 division rounding (Vulkan permits 2.5 ulp; measured 1 on Metal, 2 on Intel ANV and AMD RADV), which the gate bounds at 2 ulp. Root ADR-2609182100 D1: the activation never returns to the host to be quantised.\", :does-not-prove \"That the generation host uses it -- host/metal_kdot.cljk still quantises on the JVM and uploads; wiring is M2. NVIDIA unmeasured for the same reason as :decode-step-submit-shape.\"} {:id :nex-n25-mini-gguf-admission, :kind :required-local-model, :command \"kbb --backend sci verify/gguf_inventory.cljk <Nex-N2.5-mini-Uncensored-IQ4_XS.gguf or its first 64 MiB>\", :requires [:kbb :nex-n25-mini-gguf-header], :expected {:architecture \"qwen35moe\", :n-tensors 733, :block-count 40, :embedding 2048, :heads 16, :kv-heads 2, :key-length 256, :value-length 256, :rope-dim 64, :rope-base 10000000, :context 262144, :experts 256, :experts-used 8, :expert-ffn 512, :shared-expert-ffn 512, :ssm {:conv 4, :d-inner 4096, :d-state 128, :heads 16, :time-step-rank 32}, :full-attention-layers [3 7 11 15 19 23 27 31 35 39], :linear-attention-layers 30, :tokenizer-model \"gpt2\", :tokenizer-pre \"qwen35\", :vocab-count 248320, :tensor-types {:iq4_xs 391, :f32 301, :q5_k 40, :q6_k 1}, :approx-weight-gib 17.432, :lm-head [\"output.weight\" [2048 248320] :q6_k], :linear-layer-tensors [\"attn_gate\" \"attn_norm\" \"attn_qkv(q5_k 2048x8192)\" \"ffn_down_exps(512x2048x256)\" \"ffn_down_shexp\" \"ffn_gate_exps\" \"ffn_gate_inp(f32 2048x256)\" \"ffn_gate_inp_shexp\" \"ffn_gate_shexp\" \"ffn_up_exps\" \"ffn_up_shexp\" \"post_attention_norm\" \"ssm_a[32]\" \"ssm_alpha(2048x32)\" \"ssm_beta(2048x32)\" \"ssm_conv1d(4x8192 f32)\" \"ssm_dt.bias[32]\" \"ssm_norm[128]\" \"ssm_out(4096x2048)\"]}, :proves [:jvm-free-gguf-header-read :nex-architecture-inventory :nex-kernel-requirements-derived-from-artifact], :measures \"The real orcarouter Nex-N2.5-mini-Uncensored IQ4_XS GGUF header (served on aiueos-6600hs-1 by the llama.cpp control host), read with kbb on node fs -- no JVM. Owner 2026-09-18: verification target is Nex, not Gemma4, and the finished path is Kotoba + amu native only. From the inventory the decode step needs: IQ4_XS and Q5_K dequant-dot (only Q4_K/Q6_K exist today), f32 router matvec + top-8 over 256 experts, packed-expert gather for 3D ffn_*_exps, gated delta-net recurrence (ssm_alpha/beta/a/dt/conv1d/norm, 16 heads x d_state 128, conv kernel 4) on 30 layers, GQA 16/2 with partial RoPE (dim 64, sections) on 10 layers, Qwen35 gpt2-style BPE tokenizer and the embedded chat template, and a 2048 x 248320 Q6_K lm_head (~417 MB per token). Root ADR-2609182100.\", :does-not-prove \"Any execution: this is checkpoint admission, the same standing Qwen4Exp has. Weight bytes are not read.\"} {:id :nex-kdot-parity, :kind :required-local-model, :command \"deno run --unstable-webgpu --allow-read verify/nex_kdot_parity.js <blk.0.attn_gate.weight bytes> <blk.0.attn_qkv.weight bytes>\", :requires [:deno-webgpu :nex-n25-mini-gguf], :expected {:tensors {\"blk.0.attn_gate.weight\" [:iq4_xs 4096 2048], \"blk.0.attn_qkv.weight\" [:q5_k 8192 2048]}, :tolerance \"1e-4 + 1e-5*|ref|\", :measured-2026-09-18 {:max-abs {:iq4_xs 5.96e-7, :q5_k 1.19e-6}, :identical-on [:m1-max :intel-b70 :amd-8060s], :kernel-ms {:m1-max {:iq4_xs 0.213, :q5_k 0.312}, :intel-b70 {:iq4_xs 0.371, :q5_k 0.717}, :amd-8060s {:iq4_xs 0.103, :q5_k 0.116}}, :gb-s {:m1-max {:iq4_xs 20.9, :q5_k 37}, :intel-b70 {:iq4_xs 12, :q5_k 16.1}, :amd-8060s {:iq4_xs 43.2, :q5_k 99}}, :nvidia :unmeasured}}, :proves [:iq4-xs-q8-k-dot-on-real-nex-weights :q5-k-q8-k-dot-on-real-nex-weights :ggml-generic-reference-parity :real-checkpoint-bytes-not-synthetic], :measures \"ggml_kdot_wg.wgsl tensor types 23 (IQ4_XS) and 13 (Q5_K), added for Nex, on the real blk.0.attn_gate and blk.0.attn_qkv tensors cut from the served IQ4_XS GGUF (offsets from verify/gguf_inventory.cljk), against JS ports of ggml_vec_dot_{iq4_xs,q5_K}_q8_K_generic with a ggml-quantised Q8_K activation. Same numbers on three backends. Kernel time from 21 dispatches per command buffer.\", :does-not-prove \"Bandwidth on Intel: at 4.5-11.5 MB the B70 reaches only 12-16 GB/s here versus 100 GB/s on the 14.7 MB Q4_K row (hypothesis: codebook lookup through a var<private> array and a small grid; the box was also serving nex). Per-backend tuning is M2b. NVIDIA unmeasured.\"} {:id :nex-moe-gather-parity, :kind :required-local-model, :command \"deno run --unstable-webgpu --allow-read verify/nex_moe_gather_parity.js <blk.0.ffn_gate_exps.weight bytes>\", :requires [:deno-webgpu :nex-n25-mini-gguf], :expected {:tensor [\"blk.0.ffn_gate_exps.weight\" :iq4_xs [2048 512 256]], :experts [0 255 7 64 128 199 31 250], :tolerance \"1e-4 + 1e-5*|ref|\", :measured-2026-09-18 {:max-abs {:shared-input 3.58e-7, :per-expert-input 2.38e-7}, :identical-on [:m1-max :intel-b70 :amd-8060s], :kernel-ms-shared {:m1-max 0.091, :intel-b70 0.322, :amd-8060s 0.063}, :gb-s-shared {:m1-max 48.9, :intel-b70 13.8, :amd-8060s 70.2}, :nvidia :unmeasured}}, :proves [:in-kernel-expert-gather-from-gpu-ids :packed-3d-expert-tensor-addressing :shared-and-per-expert-input-modes :real-nex-expert-weights], :measures \"shaders/ggml_kdot_moe.wgsl reads the eight selected expert ids from a storage buffer and addresses the packed [cols, rows, 256] tensor in-kernel, so the router`s top-k never returns to the host (root ADR-2609182100 D1). Verified on the real blk.0.ffn_gate_exps.weight (142.6 MB, 256 experts x 512 rows) for eight experts including the first and last slice, in both input modes, against the JS port of ggml_vec_dot_iq4_xs_q8_K_generic on each expert`s own slice.\", :does-not-prove \"The router itself (f32 matvec + softmax + top-8 + weight normalisation) and the weighted sum