(2 kv), 32 v-heads x 128, conv 8192 channels k=4, 256 experts top-8, vocab 248320\", :tolerance \"1e-5 abs + 1e-5 rel (rope 1e-4, attn 2e-5), top-k ids exact, argmax exact\", :measured-2026-09-18 {:all-pass-on [:m1-max :intel-b70 :amd-8060s], :topk-ids [95 132 245 148 118 235 177 83], :nvidia :unmeasured}}, :proves [:qwen35moe-decode-step-elementwise-ops :moe-router-softmax-topk-on-gpu :conv1d-ring-state-on-gpu :neox-partial-rope :gqa-decode-attention-with-attn-gate :two-stage-argmax-over-full-vocab :one-module-many-entry-points-one-bind-layout], :measures \"shaders/nex_ops.wgsl -- every non-matvec op of one qwen35moe decode step as one WGSL module with one entry point each and one explicit 7-slot bind-group layout, so a step can be recorded into one command buffer -- against f64 JS references of the llama.cpp src/models/qwen35moe.cpp graph semantics (build_norm RMS, build_gdn_l2_norm, build_norm_gated, LLM_FFN_SILU/PAR, ggml_ssm_conv + silu, build_moe_ffn SOFTMAX + norm_w, softplus(alpha+dt)*A and sigmoid(beta), weighted expert sum + sigmoid shared gate, ggml_rope_multi as NEOX on n_rot for text, build_attn one-query GQA then * sigmoid(gate), greedy argmax) at Nex shapes.\", :does-not-prove \"Composition into a real decode step, tokenizer, or parity with llama.cpp on real weights: the full 17.4 GB GGUF does not fit beside the serving llama-server on any fleet GPU, so the composed step needs a node with the control host stopped (owner) or a second card. Timings here are single submits (13 ms floor) and are not kernel times.\"} {:id :nex-decode-step-parity, :kind :required-local-model, :command \"deno run --unstable-webgpu --allow-read --allow-env verify/nex_decode_step.js <Nex-N2.5-mini-Uncensored-IQ4_XS.gguf> 760,6511,314,9338,369 8 11751,13,220,97034,95779,103725,95895,9398\", :requires [:deno-webgpu :nex-n25-mini-gguf :gpu-memory-24gib], :expected {:weights-gb 18.45, :submits-per-token 1, :prompt-ids [760 6511 314 9338 369], :first-two-greedy-tokens [11751 13], :top8-after-prompt {:kotodama [11751 264 524 279 799 10919 3750 16138], :llamacpp-metal-master [11751 264 524 279 799 10919 3750 16138], :llamacpp-vulkan-b10883-b70 [11751 264 279 524 799 3750 1076 10919]}, :logprob-gap-top1-top2 {:kotodama 1.722, :llamacpp-metal 1.723, :llamacpp-vulkan 1.687}, :measured-2026-09-18 {:m1-max {:ms-per-token-median 51.8, :gpu-only-ms-per-token 39.7, :ms-per-token-median-r1-only 68.1, :tok-s 19.3, :gpu-tok-s 25.2, :llamacpp-metal-tok-s 56.5, :submit-readback-floor-ms 12, :dispatches-per-token 847}, :greedy-divergence-at-step 3, :greedy-divergent-token \"<|im_end|> (248046) where Vulkan b10883 emitted 220; llama.cpp Metal master stopped at EOG after 3 tokens, i.e. also chose <|im_end|>\"}}, :proves [:full-qwen35moe-decode-on-gpu :one-command-buffer-per-token :token-id-only-readback :distribution-parity-with-llamacpp :f32-activation-dot-matches-gpu-llamacpp], :measures \"verify/nex_decode_step.js: all 40 Nex layers (30 delta-net + 10 GQA), MoE with in-kernel expert gather, lm_head in 4 chunks, argmax -- weights streamed from the served GGUF (18.45 GB incl. token_embd) into GPU buffers, one command buffer per token with one token-id readback. Correctness: layer 0 (two tokens, state carry) and layer 3 (attention, position 1) match an f64 CPU reference from dequantised weights to ~1e-6 relative at every stage (verify/nex_layer0_reference.js); after the 5-token prompt the top-8 next-token set and order equal llama.cpp Metal master exactly, and the top-1/top-2 logprob gap matches both llama.cpp builds to 0.04; greedy tokens match the B70 Vulkan control host for the first two, then diverge on a near-tie (<|im_end|> vs space) that llama.cpp`s own Metal and Vulkan builds also disagree on.\", :does-not-prove \"Speed parity: 68 ms/token on M1 Max vs llama.cpp Metal 56.5 tok/s (3.9x). B70 numbers need the serving llama-server stopped (owner). Tokenizer and chat template are not in this harness (prompt and reference are token ids from llama.cpp`s /tokenize and /completion). Deno WebGPU is the harness, not the runtime.\"} {:id :kdot-f32-layouts, :kind :required-local-model, :command \"deno run --unstable-webgpu --allow-read verify/kdot_f32_bench.js <attn_gate.iq4xs.bin> <attn_qkv.q5k.bin> <ffn_gate_exps.iq4xs.bin>\", :requires [:deno-webgpu :nex-n25-mini-gguf], :expected {:layouts [:r1 :r8 :v3 :v3b :v3c], :parity-excess-max 1e-4, :timing \"GPU timestamp queries on Metal; host delta over 40 dispatches on Vulkan (wgpu returned raw ticks there)\", :gb-s-2026-09-18-40-dispatch {:intel-b70 {:q5_k {:r1 106, :r8 137, :v3 224, :v3b 183, :v3c 208}, :iq4_xs-gate {:r1 23, :v3 48, :v3b 57, :v3c 54}, :iq4_xs-experts {:r1 36, :v3 55, :v3b 62, :v3c 72}}, :amd-8060s {:q5_k {:r1 131, :r8 136, :v3 135, :v3b 136}, :iq4_xs-gate {:r1 67, :r8 65, :v3 67}, :iq4_xs-experts {:r1 108, :r8 117, :v3 58}}, :m1-max-gpu-timestamps {:q5_k {:r1 18, :r8 22, :v3 23, :v3b 22}, :iq4_xs-gate {:r1 15, :v3b 40, :v3c 37}, :iq4_xs-experts {:r1 17, :v3b 38, :v3c 38}}}, :gb-s-2026-09-18-first-pass {:intel-b70 {:q5_k {:r1 22, :r8 108, :v3 162, :v3b 94}, :iq4_xs-gate {:r1 13, :v3 24, :v3b 30}, :iq4_xs-experts {:r1 29, :v3 37, :v3b 54}}, :amd-8060s {:q5_k {:r1 92, :r8 151, :v3 85, :v3b 88}, :iq4_xs-gate {:r1 51, :v3b 60}, :iq4_xs-experts {:r1 81, :v3b 54}}, :m1-max {:q5_k {:r1 22, :r8 26, :v3b 29}, :iq4_xs-gate {:r1 19, :v3 34, :v3b 40}, :iq4_xs-experts {:r1 13, :v3b 40}}, :nvidia :unmeasured}, :table {:intel {:q5_k :v3, :iq4_xs :v3c}, :amd {:q5_k :r8, :iq4_xs :r8}, :metal {:q5_k :v3, :iq4_xs :v3b}}, :composed-step-m1-max {:before-ms 68.1, :after-layouts-ms 54.2, :after-fusion-ms 51.8, :gpu-only-ms-per-token 39.7, :gpu-tok-s 25.2, :dispatches-per-token {:before 1067, :after 847}, :host-floor-ms 12}, :subgroups \"blocked: Naga in Deno`s wgpu rejects `enable subgroups` (wgpu#5555); shader-f16 and timestamp-query are available\"}, :proves [:same-arithmetic-four-layouts :per-backend-per-type-kernel-choice :no-backend-is-the-reference :x-staged-in-workgroup-memory :codebook-staged-in-workgroup-memory], :measures \"Four layouts of the f32-activation K-quant dot on the real blk.0.attn_gate (IQ4_XS), blk.0.attn_qkv (Q5_K) and blk.0.ffn_gate_exps (8 experts) tensors, all four within 1e-4 of each other, timed as 21 dispatches per command buffer. The fastest layout differs by backend and by type -- Intel wants the sub-block-per-thread v3 for Q5_K (7.4x over r1) but the shared-codebook v3b for IQ4_XS, AMD wants r8 for Q5_K and r1 for IQ4_XS, Metal wants v3b -- so verify/nex_decode_step.js carries a (backend, type) -> layout table and picks at bind-group build. With it the composed step on M1 Max went 68.1 -> 54.2 ms/token.\", :does-not-prove \"Bandwidth parity: the best IQ4_XS layout is still 30-60 GB/s on every backend against 100-160 for Q5_K/Q4_K, and Metal tops out near 40 GB/s where llama.cpp reaches ~200 (simdgroup kernels). NVIDIA unmeasured.\"}]",
