  "[{:id :gemma4-num-native, :status :not-yet, :reason \"The real 42-layer PLE host, KV cache, tokenizer, and dense output projection execute. Native JDK-FFM mmap K-dot and persistent Deno WebGPU→Metal K-dot both match the official ggml Q8_K/Q4_K/Q6_K oracle; the fixed probe matches live Ollama exactly (token 9079, ` Paris`). Apple M4 Metal preserves two-token ` Paris.` generation and a [10240,2560] Q4_K projection measures about 15–20 ms, but warm decode is 8.4 s/token after shared Q/K/V and gate/up transactions, but attention/MLP/PLE stage outputs are still read back and RMSNorm/attention/MLP/PLE remain JVM-side. Measured 2026-08-13 on a prompt OUTSIDE the fixed probe -- `The largest planet in our solar system is` -- the 42-block PLE path generated ` Jupiter. Jupiter is a gas` with its first token identical to live Ollama 0.31.1 greedy (`Jupiter`), so the deep-layer drift reported by murakumo-studio in July is gone; that is one prompt at six tokens, evidence rather than logit-level parity, which remains incomplete. Those six tokens took 6.9-15.5 s each with load average moving between roughly 8 and 176 from unrelated processes, so they do not restate the 8.4 s/token figure. Full-layer GPU residency/fusion beyond grouped projections, broad prompt/logit parity, continuous batching, multi-model scheduling, and Ollama pull/push/copy/delete/chat/embedding API breadth remain incomplete. A compatible generate/tags/show/ps/version HTTP server now has loopback streaming and persistent-session tests.\"} {:id :distributed-llm-vllm-like, :status :partial, :reason \"Distributed transformer specs carry tensor/pipeline parallelism, shard strategy, and paged KV cache as EDN. THE DECISIONS ARE NO LONGER CONTRACT-ONLY: kotoba/scheduler_core.kotoba exports seventeen of them -- paged-KV block accounting and the vLLM watermark (P3), chunked prefill, admission and preemption rank (P4), prefix-cache reuse and speculative accept/emit (P5) -- each with a test-* export that amu runs on the JVM KIR oracle, wasm32 and aarch64, and a host mirror in cljc/src/kotodama/inference/scheduler.cljk that scheduler_parity_test checks against it. What is still absent is the SERVER: the aggregates those decisions decide over (block table, sequence list, radix trie), remote worker execution, and any measured throughput. A decision table is not a scheduler, and the split is deliberate rather than partial work -- the host owns the aggregates because a native export cannot take a handle.\"} {:id :kotoba-native-inference-path, :status :partial, :reason \"The owner's direction is inference with no vLLM, Ollama, MLX or llama.cpp underneath -- kotoba CLI and the amu native binary only -- and this entry is what that is measured against, because the gates above are built on the Ollama surface and do not measure it. Landed 2026-09-09 and executed as real processes on both ISAs: kernel-dot-f32 and Q8_0's fused dequantize-and-dot now have AArch64 arms (kotoba-native 7cbed512, kotoba-mir b70a567a), each the x86 SCALAR arm reproduced instruction for instruction because the contract of those operations is an accumulation tree and not a dot product; a hosted native target may now read a REGION ITS CALLER GRANTED (kotoba-verifier 33b3d067, artifact b5a7c9c5, kototama-native 9e53ea35), which is the primitive the provider CLI's generate! refuses on today as :kotodama/blocked-on :kotoba/bytes-access. Measured: 64 granted bytes fold to 2080 on aarch64 and x86_64 identically; a fixture whose answer names the tree answers 0x4B80000C where a left-to-right sum answers 0x4B800000. Still absent: Q4_K and Q6_K AArch64 arms (their thirty-two groups are unrolled with per-group geometry, so it is not a port), the four codebook formats on either backend, a transport for regions larger than argv allows, and the decision to move the provider CLI's runtime from wasm32 to this native path. No token has been generated through it. A GATE EXISTS FOR IT NOW (:kotoba-native-executed above) and it runs `npm run conformance` in ../amu, which compiles Kotoba with amu, builds the kexe loader and EXECUTES the artifact under W^X on the host ISA -- 407 seconds, measured. It is the first gate in this ledger that measures the owner`s direction rather than the portable contract or the Ollama-compatible surface this repository SERVES. It does not reach the cross-ISA bit-identity assertions, which live in amu`s own isa_execution_test and run there on both ISAs as real processes.\"} {:id :mtp-llm, :status :partial, :reason \"Qwen3.8-Flash-Next now has fail-closed official checkpoint admission for all 31 MTP tensors, a continuous-generation draft/target step, device-resident multi-row rejection verification, and acceptance metrics. The Qwen4Exp MTP decoder layer weight loader and forward pass, real-token parity, and end-to-end throughput evidence are still incomplete; metadata admission must not be reported as model execution.\"} {:id :diffusion-onix-like, :status :contract-only, :reason \"Diffusion specs now model text encoder, denoiser, VAE decoder, and scheduler selection over torch/num, but real UNet/VAE weight loading, scheduler stepping, image latent sampling, and browser WebGPU image generation are not implemented yet.\"} {:id :audio-whisper-like, :status :contract-only, :reason \"Audio specs now model feature extraction, audio encoder, and text decoder over torch/num, but real Whisper-like log-mel extraction, encoder/decoder weights, timestamp decoding, and streaming transcription are not implemented yet.\"} {:id :browser-real-model-webgpu, :status :not-yet, :reason \"browser wasm/WebGPU matmul and capability surfaces build, but real model token generation in browser over num/wgsl is not yet implemented.\"} {:id :webgl-host, :status :host-required, :reason \"WebGL remains a host-provided num-compatible backend, not implemented in Rust wgpu.\"} {:id :nex-decode-step, :status :partial, :reason \"2026-09-18: a full Nex-N2.5-mini decode runs on the GPU as one command buffer per token from the served GGUF and agrees with llama.cpp at the next-token distribution level (gate :nex-decode-step-parity). Still absent: speed (68 ms/token on M1 Max, 3.9x behind llama.cpp Metal -- the K-quant dot reaches 51 GB/s there and 12-17 GB/s on Intel for IQ4_XS/Q5_K), the tokenizer and chat template, batching, the B70 measurement, and the finished path itself: this harness is Deno WebGPU, and the owner`s requirement is Kotoba + amu native only.\"}]"}]
